source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
Write one decision's value into ink.toml.

Usage: ink pin [OPTIONS] <PATH>...

Arguments
  <PATH>...  A decision, addressed `[PATH] CODE`: a file's path and a code
             (`posts/a.md page.title`), or a site code alone (`site.title`)

Options
      --dry-run  Print the pin and write nothing

Source
      --source <KIND>  `folder` reads the files on disk, `git` reads a commit
                       [default: `git` when .git exists, said as a notice]
      --rev <REV>      The commit to read, as `git rev-parse` takes it; only for
                       a git repository [default: HEAD]

Global  -C, --json, -q, -v, --color, --no-progress, --log, --log-file
        (see `ink --help`)
More    ink pin --help adds examples, notes and exit codes
